<td id="A2.T2.2.18.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">1000</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>StrongReject-Harmful</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This dataset comprises <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="313" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">313</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">313</annotation></semantics></math> harmful prompts across six categories.
Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.2 StrongReject-Harmful ‣ Appendix B Dataset Splits and Categories ‣ RepIt: Representing Isolated Targets to Steer Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the splits.</p>
</div>
